# What belongs in this repo
#
# Only the six loader/version source trees and the shared docs. Everything else in the
# working folder - the Additions project, OLD/, BACKUP/, the dated backups, RELEASES/,
# scratch folders - stays local. Top-level is an allowlist so nothing slips in by accident.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/INTEGRATION.md

# Promo screenshots for the CurseForge/Modrinth listings. One shared copy, deliberately
# OUTSIDE every tree's src/main/resources so they are never packaged into the jars.
!/promo/
!/Fabric 1.20.1/
!/Fabric 1.21.1/
!/Forge 1.20.1/
!/Forge 1.21.1/
!/Neoforge 1.20.1/
!/Neoforge 1.21.1/

# Build output and local state, per tree
build/
.gradle/
run/
runs/
runClient/
runServer/
out/
bin/
*.iml
.idea/
.eclipse/
.settings/

# Reference copies of OTHER PEOPLE'S code, extracted at each tree's root for writing the
# reflection bridges against. Not ours to redistribute, and not build inputs - the build
# takes these from libs/*.jar via compileOnly. The paths are anchored one level down so they
# cannot touch src/main/java/net.
/*/net/
/*/weather2/
/*/sereneseasons/

# Third-party mod jars used as compileOnly dependencies.
# Not ours to redistribute - see README for which jars each tree expects in its libs/.
libs/

# Dated snapshot folders left by earlier edit passes, at root or nested in a tree.
# Git history is the backup now.
_*backup*/

# Empty 0-byte files left by a stray shell redirect
/*/Compilation
/*/Task

# Internal dev notes - port-progress trackers, conversion references and the AI task prompts
# used during the Fabric/NeoForge conversions. Kept on disk, not in the repo: they describe
# process rather than the mod, and the PROMPT files contain local filesystem paths.
# INTEGRATION.md is deliberately NOT here - it is written for outside mod and datapack authors.
/*/README.md
/*/NEOFORGE_CONVERSION.md
/*/NEOFORGE_CONVERSION_PROMPT.md

# Claude Code session state
.claude/

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
